Z||000000||FieroGT||11-05-1999||02:50 PM||||My question to everyone:<P>Provided that Cliff is willing to accommodate this, is anyone interested in having a section of the forum for completely off-topic posts? I mean posts that are not Fiero-related at all. Soemtimes it's a good way for everyone to interact and get to know other members better. Thoughts on this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||11-05-1999||04:47 PM||||Do you know that Cliff pays for this forum out of his own pocket? I don't think we should push his pocket book any more.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||11-05-1999||04:51 PM||||I've actually thought about this. Since we all have one thing in common - we're all Fiero nuts - chances are there might be more interests we share.<P>The quickest way to find out if people would be interested in such a section, is for me to send out an email to all members and give people the chance to reply with their vote. <P>I'm all for an "Off-topic" section, but I will only create one if the majority thinks it's a good idea.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000003||mrfixit58||11-05-1999||05:00 PM||||Sure! Why not? The great thing about Cliff's forum is you can read what you want and ignore the rest.<P>Got my vote "yes".||||reg||14
Z||000004||FieroGT||11-05-1999||05:03 PM||||I think that the vote is an excellent idea, Cliff. I'm looking forward to casting my ballot. <P>So, when's the election, Cliff? :')<p>[This message has been edited by FieroGT (edited 11-05-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||11-05-1999||05:06 PM||||PS: Phil, don't worry about the costs, I've got the space on my servers and the bandwidth to boot. It's true I pay this forum out of my own pocket but remember how much I've been saving because of all of the wonderful advise I find here! Not to mention the fun I'm having... I love reading all the posts! There aren't many discussion forums out there with almost 600 members where they all get along so well and display such a great sense of humor!||||reg||7
